# Winged Stallion — a Two-color greater enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 7/12 Two-color greater enemies — 20 life, bribe 100 gold
# enemy: Winged Stallion (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0127.dck "Winged Stallion (U/W, 4th)" [Tier 3 —
#   Manalink 3 file dated 2016-02-15; its first 16 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 16
#   lines (60 cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/winged_stallion.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level
#   7) [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/winged_stallion.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Greater) — "Winged Stallion"
#   (Original) [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Winged Stallion
12 Plains
12 Island
3 Howling Mine
3 Island Sanctuary
4 Mesa Pegasus
2 Phantasmal Forces
2 Serra Angel
2 Dancing Scimitar
4 Magical Hack
2 Karma
2 Lifetap
4 Psionic Entity
3 Holy Armor
3 Holy Strength
2 Segovian Leviathan
1 Disenchant
1 Conversion
2 Counterspell
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   1 Conversion, 2 Counterspell
#   .vBlack  3 Counterspell
#   .vBlue   3 Counterspell
#   .vGreen  3 Counterspell
#   .vRed    2 Conversion, 1 Counterspell
#   .vWhite  3 Counterspell
SB: 1 Counterspell
SB: 1 Conversion
